WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:05.280
Trying to stay healthy can seem&nbsp;
like a full-time job sometimes.&nbsp;

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:08.960
Especially with all the conflicting&nbsp;
information that’s out there.&nbsp;

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:12.880
But, I’m here to make that job a little easier.&nbsp;

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:17.760
Welcome to the Nutrition Facts podcast,&nbsp;
I’m your host Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:22.400
Did you know that a single dietary change&nbsp;
can increase our resting metabolic rate?&nbsp;

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:27.040
Here’s our story with Nutrition Facts Senior&nbsp;
Research Scientist: Dr. Kristine Dennis.

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:29.440
We now know why fiber-rich foods

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:31.680
can have such a powerful effect
on our weight.

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:34.000
The evidence for the role
of fiber in weight control

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.720
started with so-called
ecological studies.

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:39.360
These involve comparing
population averages,

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:40.480
and researchers noted

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:42.960
that populations
with extraordinary fiber intakes

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:45.920
tend to have
negligible obesity rates.

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:48.480
For example, the average
Pima Indian in Mexico

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:50.240
eating their traditional
high-fiber diet

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:51.920
centered around
the "three sisters"

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:53.600
(corn, beans, and squash)

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:55.200
is normal weight,

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:59.520
but the average Pima on U.S.
reservations has obesity.

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:01.760
The problem with dealing
with population averages

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:02.560
is that we don’t know

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:04.880
if the individuals eating
the higher-fiber diets

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:08.880
are themselves necessarily
the ones protected from obesity.

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:10.320
What do we see
in cohort studies,

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:13.520
where individuals and their
diets are followed over time?

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:15.520
A cohort study
of overweight youth found

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:16.800
that the amount of fiber found

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:19.520
in a single half cup
daily serving of beans,

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:21.200
about 6 grams,

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:22.800
over about a two-year period,

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:25.760
was associated
with a profound 25% difference

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:28.480
in abdominal obesity.

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:30.160
In about the same timeframe,

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:31.360
in middle-aged women,

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:33.520
each 2-gram increase
in daily fiber

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:35.520
was associated
with a weight decrease

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:38.400
of about a pound (0.45 kg).

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:40.560
The postpartum period
seems to be a critical time

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:42.160
for women to be
at risk of retaining

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:44.640
the weight put on
during pregnancy.

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:46.240
A study of hundreds of new moms

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:48.000
followed for the first
five months

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:49.920
found that inadequate
fiber intake

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:53.280
appeared to increase
obesity risk by 24%.

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:55.200
And it’s not just women.

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:57.600
A cohort that included
tens of thousands of men

00:01:57.600 --> 00:01:58.880
followed for years

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:01.120
concluded that an increase
in fiber consumption

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:02.880
of just 10 grams a day

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:06.720
may prevent about 10% of weight
gain within the population.

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:09.600
Overall, the evidence from these
kinds of observational studies

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:10.640
is strong that

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:12.560
"Increasing consumption
of dietary fiber

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:15.600
with fruits, vegetables,
whole grains, and legumes

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:17.040
across the life cycle

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:20.240
is a critical step in stemming
the epidemic of obesity."

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:22.800
These studies can control
for nondietary influences

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:24.400
such as physical activity

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:27.360
by equipping people with gadgets
to measure their movement,

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:30.560
but there may be uncontrolled
confounding dietary factors.

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:33.360
Think about the list
of high-fiber foods--

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:36.480
fruits, vegetables,
whole grains, and beans.

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:37.840
Maybe fiber intake is just

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:40.800
a marker for the intake
of healthy foods,

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:43.440
and there are dozens of reasons
why eating whole plant foods

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:47.040
could lead to weight loss that
have nothing to do with fiber.

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:49.040
To know if there’s
a cause-and-effect relationship

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:51.440
between fiber and weight loss,

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:55.040
you need to put it to the test
in interventional trials.

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:58.000
That’s where colonic infusions
can come in handy.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:02:59.280
In a randomized, double-blind,

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:01.200
placebo-controlled
crossover study,

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:04.160
researchers showed that people’s
metabolism can be boosted

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:06.800
within 30 minutes of
an infusion into their rectums

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:08.320
of short-chain fatty acids,

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:12.480
the molecules our gut bacteria
make when we feed them fiber.

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:15.280
The study used the amounts
we’d expect to create ourselves

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:17.440
just from eating
a high-fiber diet.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:20.240
Not only did the study
participants get an increase

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:22.000
in their resting metabolic rate

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:24.880
(the amount of calories burned
just by existing),

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:28.240
but specifically, their fat
oxidation shot up as well,

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:29.840
increasing the amount
of fat they were burning

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:32.560
by more than 25%.

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:33.680
This translates to about

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:36.400
an extra third of a pat
of butter’s worth of fat

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:40.160
burned off their body within
two hours of the infusion.

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:42.000
Colonic catheters aside,

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:44.320
we can get short-chain
fatty acids directly

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:45.600
and get the same little bump

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:49.120
in resting metabolic rate
and whole-body fat breakdown

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:52.000
in addition
to a decrease in appetite.

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:54.320
So again, fiber may work
on both sides

00:03:54.320 --> 00:03:56.000
of the energy balance equation.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:57.600
But does that decreased appetite

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:00.080
actually translate
into eating less?

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:03.440
We’ll find out next.

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:05.280
How does the fiber
we eat in foods

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:08.000
impact our appetites
and our resting metabolic rate,

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:11.280
the amount of calories burned
just by existing?

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:16.080
What happens when we eat
fiber-filled foods like beans?

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:18.480
Researchers in Sweden gave
people beans for supper,

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:19.760
and by the next morning,

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:22.800
after their friendly flora had
a chance to eat them too,

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:25.760
their satiety hormones
like PYY were up,

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:28.560
their hunger hormone ghrelin
was down,

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:32.240
and they reported
feeling less hungry.

00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:35.120
The researchers didn’t measure
subsequent food intake,

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:39.040
but a similar study with
whole-grain rye for supper did

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:42.560
and found a decrease in food
intake at lunch the next day.

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:44.960
Those who had eaten the
fiber-rich food the night before

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:48.960
felt fully satiated with about a
hundred fewer calories at a meal

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:51.840
more than 12 hours later.

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:53.440
So, by eating fiber-rich foods,

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:56.080
you’re setting yourself up
for success.

00:04:56.880 --> 00:04:58.880
Reduced caloric intake
at a single meal,

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:00.560
or even over a whole day,

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:01.600
doesn’t necessarily translate

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:03.360
into long-term weight loss,
though,

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:07.280
as our body may find
ways of compensating.

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:09.440
Experimentally delivering
short-chain fatty acids

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:11.600
directly to the colon
every day for months

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:13.760
does reduce abdominal fat,
liver fat,

00:05:13.760 --> 00:05:15.440
and overall weight gain.

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:18.080
But what about getting them
the old-fashioned way,

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:20.960
eating fiber through our mouth?

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:24.240
A 2022 systematic review
and meta-analysis compilation

00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:26.720
of more than two dozen
randomized controlled trials

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:30.560
of various straight fiber
supplements versus placebo

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:32.080
found that those
study participants

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:34.640
in the groups taking
the actual fiber

00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:37.040
lost an average of about two
and a half pounds (1.25 kg) more

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:39.040
than those
in the control groups.

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:42.000
These were studies only
averaging 17 weeks long,

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:44.000
though there have been fiber
supplementation trials

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:45.760
that have lasted up to a year,

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:48.160
and they showed
significantly more weight loss.

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:50.880
The fiber supplement findings
were inconsistent, however,

00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:53.520
presumably because dozens
of different fiber types

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:55.120
were tested.

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:58.480
How much money can you make
selling beans?

00:05:58.480 --> 00:06:00.960
So, there are all sorts of fancy
new fibers on the market

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:05.200
with names like "IQP G-002AS."

00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:07.440
(The IQP stands for InQpharm,

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:10.000
the drug company
that came up with it.)

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:12.320
Ironically, it was found
to be quite effective--

00:06:12.320 --> 00:06:15.440
according, of course, to the
employees of said drug company,

00:06:15.440 --> 00:06:17.040
who published the study.

00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:20.320
Using isolated fiber
extracted from plants

00:06:20.320 --> 00:06:21.440
or made in a lab

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:24.640
can be helpful in experimentally
proving fiber’s effectiveness

00:06:24.640 --> 00:06:28.560
apart from all the other healthy
components in whole foods.

00:06:28.560 --> 00:06:31.200
But if anything, one might
expect even greater benefits

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:33.360
from eating fiber
the way nature intended,

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:35.600
in intact plant foods.

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:36.960
It turns out that telling people

00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:38.800
to increase their intake
of fiber-rich foods

00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:40.400
may actually be
one of the most effective

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:43.520
single pieces of advice
for weight loss.

00:06:43.520 --> 00:06:46.000
Published in the prestigious
Annals of Internal Medicine,

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:46.960
a study entitled

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:50.240
"Single-Component Versus
Multicomponent Dietary Goals"

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:52.000
randomly assigned
hundreds of people

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:55.200
into one of two
weight-loss regimens.

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:56.400
One simply encouraged people

00:06:56.400 --> 00:06:59.280
to get at least 30 grams
of fiber each day,

00:06:59.280 --> 00:07:02.320
which is about the recommended
minimum adequate intake.

00:07:02.320 --> 00:07:03.600
The other group was advised

00:07:03.600 --> 00:07:06.160
to follow a far more complex
weight-loss program

00:07:06.160 --> 00:07:09.120
recommended by
the American Heart Association.

00:07:09.120 --> 00:07:11.040
In addition to also
being advised to hit

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:13.600
the 30 daily grams of fiber
target,

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:15.200
study participants
were prescribed

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:17.600
carefully calculated
calorie intake goals,

00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:20.400
told to switch
from red meat to white,

00:07:20.400 --> 00:07:22.000
cut down on sugary beverages,

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:24.640
reduce sugar and sodium intake
across the board,

00:07:24.640 --> 00:07:27.440
and moderate
their alcohol intake.

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:30.000
Even though
both groups were told

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:31.840
to reach the same fiber target,

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:34.080
the group whose sole focus
was fiber intake

00:07:34.080 --> 00:07:36.640
ended up eating more than
twice as much extra fiber

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:39.120
as the multicomponent
intervention,

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:40.400
and surprisingly,

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:43.360
similarly improved
the quality of their diets.

00:07:43.360 --> 00:07:45.680
So, the fiber-only group
ended up reducing

00:07:45.680 --> 00:07:47.760
their saturated fat intake
as much as the group

00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:50.480
who was explicitly
instructed to do so.

00:07:50.480 --> 00:07:52.560
Just telling people
to eat more whole plant foods

00:07:52.560 --> 00:07:55.040
seems by default
to naturally crowd out

00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:56.800
some of the less healthy options

00:07:56.800 --> 00:07:59.760
that may have ended up
on their plates.

00:07:59.760 --> 00:08:01.600
With similar
dietary improvements,

00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:03.920
both groups lost
similar amounts of weight,

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:04.960
suggesting if you were able

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:07.600
to give only one piece
of weight-loss advice,

00:08:07.600 --> 00:08:10.960
eating more fiber
might not be a bad choice.

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:13.840
Of course, it only works
if you actually do it.

00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:16.400
One low-carb study reported
favorable results

00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:19.040
compared to a "high-fiber" diet.

00:08:19.040 --> 00:08:22.720
How high was this so-called
high-fiber diet?

00:08:22.720 --> 00:08:24.240
The study participants
started out

00:08:24.240 --> 00:08:27.920
at a terribly low
17.4 grams a day.

00:08:27.920 --> 00:08:30.880
Unfortunately, that’s pretty
typical for the United States.

00:08:30.880 --> 00:08:32.800
That’s only about half
the average recommended

00:08:32.800 --> 00:08:36.480
minimum daily intake
of 31.5 grams.

00:08:36.480 --> 00:08:38.480
The human body
was designed to consume

00:08:38.480 --> 00:08:41.600
more than 100 grams of fiber
a day.

00:08:41.600 --> 00:08:44.400
The participants started out
at 17.4 grams,

00:08:44.400 --> 00:08:50.160
and on their "high-fiber" diet,
shot up to 19.7 grams.

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:52.880
That is in no way
a high-fiber diet,

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:55.440
yet the researchers used
their findings to conclude,

00:08:55.440 --> 00:08:57.920
"we believe previous claims
of the benefits of fiber

00:08:57.920 --> 00:09:00.720
for weight loss
may have been overstated."

00:09:00.720 --> 00:09:03.440
Less than 3% of Americans
reach even the recommended

00:09:03.440 --> 00:09:05.840
minimum daily
adequate intake of fiber.

00:09:05.840 --> 00:09:07.920
There’s so much fuss
about protein,

00:09:07.920 --> 00:09:10.320
but for that,
the stats are reversed:

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:13.600
More than 97% of Americans
do get enough protein,

00:09:13.600 --> 00:09:18.640
and more than 97% of Americans
do not get enough fiber.

00:09:18.640 --> 00:09:21.200
Almost everyone is eating
fiber-deficient diets,

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:22.160
and that’s just based

00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:25.040
on the piddly U.S.
dietary recommendations

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:27.680
of 14 grams
per thousand calories,

00:09:27.680 --> 00:09:31.200
which comes out to be
about 25 g/day for women

00:09:31.200 --> 00:09:34.320
and 38 g/day for men.

